condition_name: Cholera
condition_slug: cholera
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: An acute severe diarrhoeal illness of worldwide importance. It is caused by Vibrio cholerae bacilli (classical and El Tor species)
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[2]: Diarrhoea (Rice water stool),Vomiting
investigations[3]: "Stool microscopy, culture and sensitivity","Urea, Electrolytes and Creatinine",Complete Blood Count
treatment:
  goals[3]: Hydration.,Eradicate organism.,Prevent spread.
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[7]: Intravenous Fluids.,Electrolyte replacement.,Oral Rehydration Therapy,"Tetracycline: Adult: 500 mg orally every 6 hours for 5 days","Doxycycline: Adult: 200 mg orally once daily for 5 days, Child: 12 - 18 years, 200 mg on first day, then 100 mg daily, Severe infections, 200 mg orally daily","Erythromycin: Adult and child over 8 years: 250 - 500 mg orally every 6 hours for 5 days or 500 mg - 1 g every 12 hours, Child: Up to 2 years: 125 mg every 6 hours, 2 - 8 years: 250 mg every 6 hours, Doses doubled in severe infection","Co-trimoxazole: Adult: 960 mg orally every 12 hours for 5 days, Child: 6 weeks - 12 years: 24 mg/kg every 12 hours, 6 weeks - 6 months: 120 mg every 12 hours, 6 months - 6 years: 240 mg every 12 hours, 6 years - 12 years: 480 mg every 12 hours, 12 years - 18 years: 960 mg every 12 hours"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[1]: "Monitor fluid intake and output (vomitus, urine and stool)"
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[3]: Hydropaenia/Hypovolaemic shock with multiple end organ failure leading to death,Dyselectrolytetaemia,Hypokalaemia
prevention[3]: Personal and communal hygiene,"Potable water, sanitary disposal of faeces",Cholera vaccine
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null